      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skia doesn\u0027t always adhere to this (especially for old tests), but I like http://engdoc/eng/doc/devguide/testing/unit/best-practices?polyglot\u003dcpp#naming \n\nWe want the test name to give a hint towards any inputs and the expected output.\n\n`DrawAntialiasHairline_SquareCappedHalfPixelOffset_SinglePixelWideOutput` is what I might call this test.\n\nNaming things like this can help point out where we might need more test coverage\n(e.g. do we need one for aliased hairlines, do we need one for a pixel-aligned hairline, etc) and gives a reader a hint as to what the test should be doing. More complicated tests can have comments explaining the test also, but the name should be a good start.",
